    "cornice": {
      "group": "envelope",
      "binding": "specified",
      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "modillion-cornice",
          "status": "forbidden",
          "note": "defining_characteristics[5] gives the house 'Clapboard or shingle wall, minimal cornice, and an end chimney', and the long description says it 'reads immediately as Colonial without requiring a portico, a cornice, or any masonry'. The record names no modillion; reading a modillioned cornice as not minimal is this binding's judgment."
        },
        {
          "id": "dentil-cornice",
          "status": "forbidden",
          "note": "The same two phrases, 'minimal cornice' and 'without requiring a portico, a cornice, or any masonry'; the record names no dentil either."
        }
      ],
      "parameters": {},
      "rule": "A minimal cornice -- 'Clapboard or shingle wall, minimal cornice, and an end chimney' (defining_characteristics[5]) -- and no modillioned or dentilled one.",
      "status": "drafted",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "judgment": true,
      "note": "BOUND 30 Sep 2026 (WP-16.2) as the companion of colonial-revival's own `cornice` binding of the same date, which makes `modillion-cornice` canonical with a 12-18 in total depth and would otherwise reach this node by descent. Until then this slot was `open` and resolved gothic-revival-british's record through colonial-revival: the modillion refused for c05's reason rather than this node's, a corbelled brick cornice canonical on a clapboard or shingle wall, and colonial-revival's 12-18 in depth merged in. This node's own words: defining_characteristics[5] reads 'Clapboard or shingle wall, minimal cornice, and an end chimney', and the long description says the house 'reads immediately as Colonial without requiring a portico, a cornice, or any masonry'. Against them stand two general sentences -- lineage[0], 'Kit, openings and entry are the parent style's; only the jettied second storey and the seventeenth-century reference differ.', and diagnostic_tells[3], 'Everything else on the house is standard Colonial Revival, including the attached garage that dates it after 1935.' -- which the specific 'minimal cornice' governs. No figure is stated, so none is carried. Marked judgment: the record says minimal and names no member, so forbidding the modillion and dentil courses is this binding's reading of the word."
    },
